WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
Four builders put up a garden wall.

2
00:00:02.510 --> 00:00:04.450
It takes them six days.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.210
The owner wants the next wall done faster.

4
00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.340
So she hires eight
builders instead of four.

5
00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:14.190
Twice the crew, so twice
the time: twelve days?

6
00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:17.850
Or take four from six and get two days?

7
00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:20.530
So how long will eight
builders really take?

8
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.740
And is that how building
sites actually work?

9
00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:26.670
In this mission, you'll
meet direct proportion,

10
00:00:26.720 --> 00:00:29.450
where more of one means more of the other.

11
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:33.380
Then inverse proportion, where more
of one means less of the other,

12
00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:35.610
and the product stays the same.

13
00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.470
You'll multiply to find
the fixed total of work,

14
00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.970
then divide, if every
builder is equally quick.

15
00:00:42.020 --> 00:00:45.710
Your mission: work out how
long eight builders would take.
